from mid-June to late July.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[0,4],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":1206,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":1126,\"text\":\"*   **Winter (December - February):** Cold, offering a more tranquil atmosphere.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[0,1,2],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":1468,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":1379,\"text\":\"Be aware that these are peak seasons, meaning larger crowds and potentially higher costs.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[5,6,7,8],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":1850,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":1615,\"text\":\"| Category | Must-See Location(s) | Cultural Significance/Highlight |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Iconic Temples** | **Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion)** | A stunning Zen temple, its top two floors covered in gold leaf, reflected in a pond.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[5,6,9,7,8],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":1995,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":1851,\"text\":\"|\\n| | **Kiyomizu-dera Temple** | Famous for its impressive 13-meter-high wooden veranda, built without a single nail, offering views over Kyoto.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[5,8],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2106,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":1996,\"text\":\"|\\n| | **Ginkaku-ji (Silver Pavilion)** | Known for its exquisite Zen garden, including the Sea of Silver Sand.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[5,7,8],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2260,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2107,\"text\":\"|\\n| **Nature & Zen** | **Tenry\u016b-ji Temple (Arashiyama)** | A leading Zen temple boasting one of the city's oldest and most celebrated landscape gardens.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[9,8],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2371,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2261,\"text\":\"|\\n| | **Ryoan-ji Temple** | Home to the world-famous rock garden, a prime example of Zen philosophy in design.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[6],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2524,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2372,\"text\":\"|\\n| **Unique Spiritual Sites**| **Fushimi Inari Taisha Shrine** | Famous for its thousands of vibrant red *torii* gates that wind up the mountain trail.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[5],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2770,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2666,\"text\":\"|\\n| **Other Key Sites** | **Sanj\u016bsangen-d\u014d** | Houses 1,001 statues of Kannon in its long wooden hall.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[9],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":2896,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2771,\"text\":\"|\\n| | **Nijo Castle** | A former residence of the Tokugawa Shogunate, featuring intricate paintings and \\\"nightingale floors.\\\"\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3043,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":2956,\"text\":\"Kyoto highly values its rich history and traditions, making cultural respect paramount.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10,11,12],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3189,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3045,\"text\":\"*   **Temples and Shrines Etiquette:**\\n    *   **Respect Sacred Spaces:** Keep your voice low; temples are places for worship and contemplation.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3404,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3194,\"text\":\"*   **Purification:** Use the *temizuya* (purification fountain) before entering: cleanse your left hand, then right, rinse your mouth (not touching the ladle to your lips), and finally, rinse the ladle handle.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10,13],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3535,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3409,\"text\":\"*   **Shoes:** Be prepared to remove your shoes before entering certain temple buildings, especially those with *tatami* mats.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10,11,14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3724,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3656,\"text\":\"Do not use a flash or take photos of worshippers without permission.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3811,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3729,\"text\":\"*   **Offerings:** Bow slightly when entering temple grounds as a sign of respect.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[10,12],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":3967,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3812,\"text\":\"*   **General Conduct:**\\n    *   **Politeness:** Use polite language like *\\\"Arigat\u014d gozaimasu\\\"* (Thank you very much) and *\\\"Sumimasen\\\"* (Pardon me/Sorry).\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[11,12],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4073,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":3972,\"text\":\"*   **Noise:** Keep your voice down in public spaces, on public transport, and especially at temples.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[13],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4161,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4078,\"text\":\"*   **Tipping:** Tipping is **not** customary in Japan; a simple \\\"thanks\\\" suffices.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[13,11,12],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4274,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4260,\"text\":\"Do not litter.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[11,14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4427,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4279,\"text\":\"*   **Geisha/Maiko:** Do not stop, follow, or act like paparazzi to photograph Geiko (Geisha) or Maiko; they are often on their way to appointments.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[15,16,17],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4853,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4727,\"text\":\"Kyoto has a good public transport network, though unlike Tokyo, buses often play a larger role in reaching specific landmarks.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[15,18],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":4986,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4855,\"text\":\"*   **Buses:** Often the **best way** to reach temples and attractions not near train/subway stations (e.g., Kinkaku-ji, Ryoan-ji).\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[15,19],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5157,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":4987,\"text\":\"Be aware of paying etiquette: generally enter at the back, exit at the front, and pay a fixed fare upon exiting (though drivers may not give change, so have coins ready).\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[15,18,19,17],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5398,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5304,\"text\":\"Local train lines (JR, Keihan, Hankyu) connect to key spots like Arashiyama and Fushimi Inari.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[15,17],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5523,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5399,\"text\":\"*   **IC Cards:** Purchase an **IC Card** (like ICOCA, Suica, or PASMO) for easy payment across nearly all public transport.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[18,16],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5694,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5662,\"text\":\"Biking is also a popular option.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5833,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5755,\"text\":\"Kyoto is generally considered an **extremely safe city** with low crime rates.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":5960,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5925,\"text\":\"Lost items are frequently returned.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6022,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":5961,\"text\":\"*   **Emergency Contacts:**\\n    *   **Police:** Dial **110**.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6072,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6027,\"text\":\"*   **Medical Emergency/Fire:** Dial **119**.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6136,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6073,\"text\":\"*   **Health/Environment:**\\n    *   Tap water is safe to drink.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[20],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6323,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6241,\"text\":\"Travel in groups and carry noise-making items if venturing far into the mountains.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[21],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6466,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6324,\"text\":\"*   **Documentation:**\\n    *   **Visas:** Check the latest requirements with the nearest Japanese embassy, as visa exemption rules can change.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[14,22],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6589,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6471,\"text\":\"*   **Insurance:** It is highly advisable to take out **travel insurance** covering medical treatment and emergencies.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[22],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6695,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6594,\"text\":\"*   **Copies:** Keep copies of important documents (passport, insurance) separate from the originals.\"}},{\"confidence_scores\":null,\"grounding_chunk_indices\":[22],\"segment\":{\"end_index\":6835,\"part_index\":null,\"start_index\":6696,\"text\":\"*   **Local Laws/Customs:** Always follow local laws, religious restrictions, and customs, particularly regarding behavior at sacred sites.\"}}],\"retrieval_metadata\":null,\"retrieval_queries\":null,\"search_entry_point\":{\"rendered_content\":\"<style>\\n.container {\\n  align-items: center;\\n  border-radius: 8px;\\n  display: flex;\\n  font-family: 